abstract: >-
  Desktop application for Windows and macOS that reproduces the analyses of the
  paper "Simulating the debris of overturning masonry façades with rigid blocks:
  from the falling panel to the documented collapses". A two-dimensional section
  of the façade overturns about its outer toe, breaks into its blocks at the
  first impact and the blocks settle on the street in the planck.js engine; the
  extent of the debris is measured as P95 by mass and Lmax. The program runs
  single walls with their animation and the total-collapse campaigns of the
  paper, and compares every run with the stored runs of the paper.
keywords:
  - masonry
  - façade
  - out-of-plane overturning
  - debris
  - rigid blocks
  - discrete element simulation
  - earthquake
  - street blockage
